{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " \"A print version of a Sudoku puzzle is available for users to view. The rules of the game are the same as traditional Sudoku, but with an added twist. Grey lines outline certain cells, and the numbers inside these cells must add up to the figures present in the corner of the shape. It is important to note that no number can be duplicated within each outlined shape. For those interested in seeing the completed puzzle, it will be featured in next week's edition of the Observer Digital Edition.\n\nAdditionallly, the Sudoku puzzle offers an extra challenge for players. Each group of cells enclosed by grey lines must add up to the target number in the corner. This means that players must use their problem-solving skills to not only fill in the missing numbers in each row and column, but also ensure that the sum of the numbers in each grey section is correct. The puzzle provides an exciting twist on the classic Sudoku game and is sure to keep players engaged.\n\nThe Observer Digital Edition will feature the completed puzzle for those who may find the game too challenging. The game is designed to test players' mental agility and problem-solving skills. With the added challenge of the grey sections, players must think strategically and plan their moves carefully to successfully complete the puzzle.\n\nFor those who are new to Sudoku, the game involves filling in a 9x9 grid with numbers from 1 to 9, with each row and column containing each number only once. The grey section rule adds an extra layer of complexity, making it a fun and engaging challenge for both new and experienced players.\n\nIn conclusion, the Sudoku puzzle offered by the Observer Digital Edition is an exciting and challenging game for players of all skill levels. With the traditional rules of Sudoku and the added challenge of the grey sections, players are sure to have a great time testing their problem-solving skills. Don't forget to check out the completed puzzle in next week's edition of the Observer Digital Edition.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.0005287918029353023}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -1.6523257493972778}, {"token": "print", "logprob": -1.0197114944458008}, {"token": "version", "logprob": -0.0011956692906096578}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -3.576272320060525e-06}, {"token": "a", "logprob": -0.06402759253978729}, {"token": "Sud", "logprob": -0.18756219744682312}, {"token": "oku", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "puzzle", "logprob": -6.985420623095706e-05}, {"token": "is", "logprob": -0.00014280252798926085}, {"token": "available", "logprob": -0.0001705739414319396}, {"token": "for", "logprob": -0.40769684314727783}, {"token": "users", "logprob": -0.8761468529701233}, {"token": "to", "logprob": -0.001865434111095965}, {"token": "view", "logprob": -0.5320775508880615}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.0015683980891481042}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.00994807854294777}, {"token": "rules", "logprob": -0.375325083732605}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.01275912206619978}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -1.0218100547790527}, {"token": "game", "logprob": -2.8729025871143676e-05}, {"token": "are", "logprob": -0.09407280385494232}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.19621171057224274}, {"token": "same", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "as", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "traditional", "logprob": -0.041216012090444565}, {"token": "Sud", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "oku", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": "but", "logprob": -0.8428153395652771}, {"token": "with", "logprob": -0.7589247226715088}, {"token": "an", "logprob": -0.1266528069972992}, {"token": "added", "logprob": -0.2938941717147827}, {"token": "twist", "logprob": -0.003779531689360738}, {"token": ".", "l